{0 workero}

Write Cloudflare Workers in OCaml (via wasm_of_ocaml).

{1 Library}

The entry point is the module {!Workero}.

{!modules: Workero}

{1 Guides}

Start with {{!page-getting_started}Getting started}. The other pages follow the
same order as a Worker project.

- {{!page-getting_started}Getting started}: prerequisites, create a project,
  develop locally, deploy.
- {{!page-handlers}Handlers}: [Workero.serve], [Workero.scheduled], and the
  arguments of a handler.
- {{!page-requests}Requests and responses}: requests, responses, URLs, JSON and
  [Workero.fetch].
- {{!page-env}Variables and secrets}.
- {{!page-async}Waiting for JavaScript}: direct style, [Promise.await] and
  background work.
- {{!page-bindings}Bindings}: {{!page-kv}KV}, {{!page-cache}Cache}, {{!page-r2}R2} and
  {{!page-d1}D1}.
- {{!page-logging}Logging}.
- {{!page-testing}Testing and limits}.
- {{!page-interop}JavaScript interop}.
- {{!page-how_it_works}How it works}: wasm_of_ocaml, JSPI, [workero build] and
  binary size.
- {{!page-libraries}Supported libraries}.
- {{!page-known_issues}Support and known issues}.
- {{!page-cli}CLI}: the [workero] command.
- {{!page-template}Template}: the starter project.
